---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this website measures about visitors, which services receive it, and how to opt out.">
  <article class="wrap prose-page">
    <p class="label label--red">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What this site measures</h1>
    <p class="updated label">Last updated 22 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use two analytics services to count visits and see which pages are read: Google Analytics 4 (run by
      Google) and PostHog (run by PostHog Inc., data stored in the United States). They receive the page address,
      the referring page, your browser and device type, an approximate location derived from your IP address, and
      an identifier stored in your browser so repeat visits can be counted.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not record sessions, keystrokes or mouse movement. PostHog session recording and automatic click capture
      are switched off in our configuration.
    </p>

    <h2>Blog views, reading time and reactions</h2>
    <p>
      Blog posts show how many times they were opened, how long readers spend on them on average, and reactions.
      These counts are kept in our own database at Supabase. Your browser sends only the post's address and a number:
      a view, a reaction, or a few seconds of reading time, counted only while the tab is visible and you are active
      on it. No IP address, cookie or identifier is stored with these counts.
    </p>
    <p>
      To count each reader once per day and remember your reaction, your browser keeps two small notes in its own
      local storage. They never leave your device. Views and reading time are not sent if your browser sends Do Not
      Track or Global Privacy Control. The counts are approximate: clearing your browser storage or using another
      device counts you again.
    </p>

    <h2>3D models</h2>
    <p>
      The semiconductors page can show interactive 3D models hosted by Sketchfab. Nothing from Sketchfab loads until you
      press "Load interactive model". After that, Sketchfab's own privacy policy applies to that frame.
    </p>

    <h2>How to opt out</h2>
    <p>
      If your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal, neither analytics service is loaded at
      all. Blocking scripts from googletagmanager.com and posthog.com has the same effect. The site works the same
      either way.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts or advertising on this site. We do not sell or share visitor data with anyone
      beyond the two services above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests about your data: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
